  "Number": 6,
  "Question": "An open box is constructed by starting with a rectangular sheet of metal \\(10\\) in. by \\(14\\) in. and cutting a square of side \\(x\\) inches from each corner. The resulting projections are folded up and the seams welded. The volume of the resulting box is:",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(140x-48x^2+4x^3\\)",
    "B": "\\(140x+48x^2+4x^3\\)",
    "C": "\\(140x+24x^2+x^3\\)",
    "D": "\\(140x-24x^2+x^3\\)",
    "E": "none of these"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "A",
  "Solution": "Each base dimension loses \\(x\\) inches at both ends, while the folded sides have height \\(x\\). Thus the box has base dimensions \\(10-2x\\) and \\(14-2x\\), in inches.\n\nVolume is length times width times height, so\n\\[\nV=x(10-2x)(14-2x)\n=x(140-48x+4x^2).\n\\]\nTherefore\n\\[\nV=140x-48x^2+4x^3\n\\]\nin cubic inches, choice \\(\\mathrm{A}\\).\n\nA nondegenerate box requires \\(0<x<5\\). At \\(x=0\\) the height vanishes, and at \\(x=5\\) the shorter base dimension vanishes.",
